\label{def:aap}An inclusion $N\subset M$ as in Proposition \ref{prop:aap}
has the Automorphism Approximation Property (AAP) relative to $Q\subset N$
if the equivalent conditions of that proposition hold. When $Q=\mathbb{C}1$,
we simply say that $N\subset M$ has AAP.

This is the standard adjoint calculation of \cite[Corollary 4.2 and Proposition 4.3]{VoiculescuEntropyV};
see also \cite[proof of Lemma 6]{ShlyakhtenkoMicrostates}. Since
$B_{0}\otimes B_{0}^{\mathrm{op}}$ is dense, $\delta$ is closable.

Write, after reindexing, $J=J'\cup\{1,2\}$. This is Theorem \ref{thm:freeProductsAbsorb}
applied to $A_{1}=C^{*}(S_{1})$, $A_{2}=C^{*}(S_{2})$ and the semicircular
family $\{S_{j}:j\in J'\}$.
